/* 69 */

<PLAYER_SETUP>
  random_placement

<LAND_GENERATION>
  base_terrain SNOW

<ELEVATION_GENERATION>


<TERRAIN_GENERATION>


<OBJECTS_GENERATION>


<CONNECTION_GENERATION>

/*
RMSTEST_57 - is the comment-opening token really the NUMBER 69?
Feeds: parser-design Sec.2.1 and Sec.13 item 7, the token-alias import

THIS HEADER IS AT THE BOTTOM. The test is the first line.

WHAT IS ALREADY MEASURED
RMSTEST_56a put the shore-fish constant alone in a leading comment and the map
came back blank; 56b without it came back snow. So that word opens a nested
comment, comments nest, and the rest of the file is never read.

WHAT IS ONLY INFERRED
That the mechanism is the NUMBER. Sec.2.1 records the community equivalencies
result - the engine resolves every word to an internal integer token id, and
constants, raw numbers and structural tokens share one id space - and our own
reference data puts that fish at 69. So the reading is that the comment-open
token is 69 and any token resolving to 69 opens a comment.

That is a chain of two steps and only the first is measured. It matters because
it decides whether the fix is "enumerate a handful of constants sharing two
known ids", which is cheap and precise, or something broader.

METHOD
The first line of this file is a comment containing nothing but the bare literal
69. If the number is the mechanism, the literal is enough - no constant needed.

  BLANK or grass map -> the number is the mechanism. The inference holds, and the
                        fix is a lookup on two ids.
  SNOW map           -> the number is NOT sufficient, so the fish is doing
                        something a bare literal does not. Then the equivalencies
                        reading is incomplete and the sweep has to be run over
                        names rather than values.

RMSTEST_56b is already the control for this - same script, comment containing
nothing at all, and it produced snow. No new control needed.

SECOND ARM, WORTH ONE MORE GENERATION
Our reference data lists a second entry at 69, an attribute constant rather than
an object. Copy this file, replace the 69 in the comment with that name, and
generate. A blank map confirms the value is what matters and the category is
not, which is the claim the cheap fix rests on. A snow map means only that one
fish is special and the whole story needs rebuilding.

STILL NOT COVERED BY EITHER ARM
The id for the comment-CLOSING token is unknown, so the constants that would end
a comment early are unenumerated. That failure is less destructive - the file
still runs, with a stretch of prose parsed as commands - but noisier, and it
needs the sheet or a search.

GENERATE AT NORMAL (200), any player count. ONE RUN. Binary.

READ IT WITH
  Look at the map. Snow or not snow is the whole reading.
*/
